 "summary": "The Hilbert-series hypothesis is exactly the form `mk_finrank_symmetricAlgebraInvariants_inf_homogeneousSubmodule_eq_sum_inv_reverse_charpoly` (Molien.lean:139) feeds, and the conclusions r = dim M, #ker\u00b7\u220fd\u1d62 = #G and #ker\u00b7\u2211(d\u1d62-1) = #pseudoreflections are faithful generalisations of Humphreys \u00a73.9. The edge cases dim M = 0, a non-faithful action, d\u1d62 = 0 and transvections (pseudoreflections with det = 1, ruled out by semisimplicity) all check out, and the auxiliary `hdet` hypothesis is discharged internally rather than smuggled into the main theorems.",
